WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.120
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:02.720
- Cross-stitch for rappers,

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:03.663
are you joking?

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:07.423
I'm an anomaly in this scene, for sure.

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.273
I'm Emma McKee, and I'm
a cross-stitch artist.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.260
I create custom, one-of-a-kind
cross-stitch jackets

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.013
for Chicago's creative class.

00:00:22.812 --> 00:00:25.130
(upbeat music)

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:28.460
Cross-stitch is a
antiquated form of stitching

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.720
traditionally done by your grandma.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.640
I fell backwards into it.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.840
I made a present for my
mom a couple years ago,

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:36.420
so I taught myself how to cross-stitch.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.020
It came very naturally to me,

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:39.030
and so

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:40.640
I decided to do more.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.950
I felt compelled to do it,

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:43.357
but I didn't know what to do it for.

00:00:43.357 --> 00:00:44.970
But then, the obvious connection was,

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:47.020
well, I'll do it for the
things that inspire me.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:50.063
And the things that I loved
were art, and poetry, and music.

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:51.743
♪ We do the ♪

00:00:51.743 --> 00:00:52.740
♪ We don't do the same drugs ♪

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.140
- Chance the Rapper is like the

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:55.380
prince of Chicago, you know?

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:57.210
He's Chicago royalty.

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.810
Chance is one of my favorite rappers,

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:00.090
and so I

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:01.190
made this jacket.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:03.420
It was a three jacket,
it was Chance's three.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:04.630
And I was like, okay,
I'll put this on Twitter.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:05.520
We'll see what this does.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:06.611
Like 30 seconds later,

00:01:06.611 --> 00:01:07.444
(phone chiming)
Chance the Rapper

00:01:07.444 --> 00:01:09.150
has followed you, Chance the
Rapper has sent you a DM.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.340
I mean, he's like, “Yo,
how do I get this?"

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:14.307
And I was like, any way
you want, Chance (laughs).

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:16.780
And he wore it on the cover of Billboard,

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:19.053
and that was kinda like how it started.

00:01:20.277 --> 00:01:21.110
(draw scraping)

00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:22.303
This, a-ha,

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:25.820
is for an artist named McJenkins.

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:26.930
It's a heart.
(upbeat music)

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:31.280
I've made something like 135
pieces in the last four years.

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:32.860
Some of the people I've made stuff for,

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.400
SZA, Major Lazer,

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.050
Chance the Rapper, Vic Mensa,

00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:36.940
Most Def,

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:37.773
Joey Purp,

00:01:37.773 --> 00:01:38.780
Kendrick Lamar.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:40.350
Oh, yeah, Lil Yachty, of course.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:42.010
How could I forget about Lil Yachty?

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:43.810
But, the majority of
them are worn by people

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:44.880
who are not famous.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.520
A lot of the people I
make stuff for in Chicago

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:48.060
wear their stuff every day.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:49.143
Live in the things.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:52.460
Cross-stitch is just a cross, stitched.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:53.540
It's just a square.

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:54.420
You basically take an image,

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.380
and you pixelate the hell out of it.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:58.570
So you map out a bunch of tiny squares.

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:00.980
It takes very good spacial recognition,

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:03.890
a lot of patience, and
you cannot mess it up.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.700
My inspiration usually will come

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.390
complete, finished,
everything, from a person.

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:10.260
It arrives in my head fully
formed, and that's it.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:11.620
I have no idea how we get there,

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:13.160
I don't sit around and
think about it for somebody.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:14.860
Like, the way that I'm able
to make something for somebody

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:15.716
is if it is there.

00:02:15.716 --> 00:02:17.465
(violin music)

00:02:17.465 --> 00:02:19.750
I have to go out to the
suburbs to buy my thread.

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:21.300
It's all specialty.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.700
I spend an ungodly amount
of money on thread,

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.082
it would freak you out.

00:02:25.082 --> 00:02:26.530
(register beeping and rattling)

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:28.890
I always say the median
amount of time in a jacket

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:31.710
is anywhere from like, 50 to 60 hours.

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.670
When you're done, then you
get to pull the graph out.

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:34.503
And then you get to see

00:02:34.503 --> 00:02:35.963
what it looks like when it's finished.

00:02:38.308 --> 00:02:39.141
(birds chirping)

00:02:39.141 --> 00:02:40.490
People call what's happening
(upbeat music)

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:41.680
in Chicago a renaissance.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:42.830
We have art, and we have music,

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:44.550
and we have all these people
making positive changes.

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.450
All these people making
incredible, incredible stuff.

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:48.870
I have a team that oscillates

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:51.410
anywhere from seven to 14 people,

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:54.040
and they're all artists, they're
all other Chicago artists.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.478
And we do these big
photo shoots with people.

00:02:56.478 --> 00:02:58.530
But it's like really the only
way that I catalog anything,

00:02:58.530 --> 00:02:59.970
is by having pictures of it.

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:00.803
- It is.

00:03:00.803 --> 00:03:01.636
- I like those a lot.

00:03:01.636 --> 00:03:03.081
The giving away part is the best part.

00:03:03.081 --> 00:03:05.541
To see something that
you've made affect somebody

00:03:05.541 --> 00:03:07.810
in what seems to be a meaningful way

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:09.065
is a pretty emotional thing.

00:03:09.065 --> 00:03:11.090
(upbeat music)

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.760
The goal with the cross-stitch jackets

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:15.270
was never to sell them or
to make money off of them.

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:17.710
It's truly, truly a passion project.

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:19.250
I'm not Gucci, I'm just, you know,

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:20.083
I'm Stitch Gawd.

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:28.950
(upbeat tone)

